WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:07.253
Hello there!

00:00:07.253 --> 00:00:09.720
Now, sometimes when we're
recording "The Slow Mo Guys,"

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:12.092
we perform the experiment --

00:00:12.092 --> 00:00:14.100
Before we perform the intro.

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:15.830
You guessed it, this
is one of those times.

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:16.663
Yeah.

00:00:16.663 --> 00:00:17.496
Can't really hide the fact

00:00:17.496 --> 00:00:19.240
that Dan has already got
himself covered in cornstarch.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:20.750
Dan, what're we doing
with this little torch?

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:22.810
So, basically I'm gonna
try fire breathing today,

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:24.440
and see what that looks like in slow mo.

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:26.360
It'll be pretty badass, I think.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:27.963
Yeah, so I'm gonna sort of--

00:00:32.318 --> 00:00:33.151
Like that.

00:00:33.151 --> 00:00:33.984
Whoa, I felt the heat on that.

00:00:33.984 --> 00:00:35.290
That was good.

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:37.112
All right, let's see what
it looks like in slow mo!

00:00:37.112 --> 00:00:38.580
Can I have some water, please?

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:39.413
Yeah.

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:42.220
All right, so what is our fuel of choice?

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:44.040
'kay, today we've got some cornstarch.

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:44.873
This is what I'd go for,

00:00:44.873 --> 00:00:47.660
because it's sort of
safer than using kerosene.

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:49.110
Cause it's not, like,
inherently flammable.

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:50.260
Dan is not a professional,

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:52.590
so we didn't wanna put
flammable liquid in his gob.

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:53.470
Yeah, I've never done it before.

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:54.360
So, basically what I'm gonna do

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:56.130
is jam as much cornstarch into my mouth

00:00:56.130 --> 00:00:57.680
as I possibly can,

00:00:57.680 --> 00:00:59.860
and then sort of blow
it out in a fine powder,

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:02.720
and then it'll deflagrate

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:04.290
by burning the next layer of material

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:06.069
and just sort of create a
big fireball, hopefully.

00:01:06.069 --> 00:01:07.150
Have you noticed that pretty much anything

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:08.590
in powder form is flammable?

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:09.740
Yeah.
Sweet, innit?

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:10.930
Yeah, just cause--

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:11.763
Even flour.

00:01:11.763 --> 00:01:13.570
It's easily burnable, and
so that's what it does.

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:15.020
It just heats up the
next layer of material

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:16.740
and just burns it, cause it's so fine.

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:17.760
All right, lets bung some in.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:18.593
Cool.

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:23.863
How's it taste?

00:02:11.981 --> 00:02:15.030
It looked like a bloody
explosion in space,

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:16.888
with stuff flying out of it.

00:02:16.888 --> 00:02:17.721
Huh.

00:02:17.721 --> 00:02:19.091
Lookit, there's your face shot.

00:02:19.091 --> 00:02:21.591
Oh, nice. When I was, like--

00:02:27.508 --> 00:02:29.008
That looks badass!

00:02:30.127 --> 00:02:33.589
That is cool!
That's cool.

00:03:00.717 --> 00:03:01.783
What's it taste like?

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:08.853
Like... corn tacos or burritos.

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:10.817
Like a tortilla.

00:03:10.817 --> 00:03:12.439
Yeah, like a tortilla.

00:03:14.039 --> 00:03:15.230
Tastes like a tortilla.

00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:17.060
All right, solid video.

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:17.910
Flames look good.

00:03:18.955 --> 00:03:19.980
Dan, you don't look good.

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:22.050
You are absolutely caked in cornstarch.

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:23.200
I think it's a good look for me.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:24.350
Yeah.

